version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
abstract: >
  Reference implementation of Hilsha Fish Migration Optimization (HFMO), a
  phase-scheduled hybrid metaheuristic for continuous, bound-constrained
  optimization inspired by the salinity-driven migration of Hilsha
  (Tenualosa ilisha) in the Bay of Bengal. The accompanying manuscript
  describing the algorithm and its benchmark evaluation is in preparation;
  this record will be updated with a DOI once it is published.
